 ## Overview
-This method voxelizes a polygonal mesh by dispatching one compute shader thread per voxel grid cell, which then tests its Axis-Aligned Bounding Box (AABB) against every triangle in the mesh using the Separating Axis Theorem (SAT) [S1, S2, S3, unofficial]. It differs from [Geometry Shader Voxelization](2566-geometry-shader-voxelization.md) by avoiding the overhead of generating geometry primitives and from [GPU Voxelization Using OpenGL Image Atomics](2544-gpu-voxelization-using-opengl-image-atomics.md) by relying on explicit geometric intersection tests rather than rasterization coverage [S2, unofficial]. It is a brute-force approach that does not use spatial acceleration structures [S2, unofficial].
